From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] venus: bind reply streams under the resource lock; free resources after unpublishing

STEAMAC-G (1.9.15, fossilize context 21, event 5b831e76): the reply
resource of a vkSetReplyCommandStreamMESA was read with fd type 1922203991,
a value no resource ever has, amid ring-resource destruction during replay
teardown. vkr_context_get_resource drops resource_mutex before the caller
reads the entry, and nothing pins it: a ring thread could look the resource
up, a destroy on the main thread could check the streams (not yet bound)
and free it, and the ring thread then read and bound freed memory. The
decoder's vkExecuteCommandStreamsMESA path had the same window between
vkr_context_destroy_resource's stream check and its free.

vkSetReplyCommandStreamMESA now looks up, checks and binds under
resource_mutex. vkr_context_destroy_resource first unpublishes the resource
(removes it from the table under resource_mutex, keeping the detach
history), then checks the context's and rings' streams, then frees it: a
concurrent bind has either completed (and is caught as before) or cannot
find the resource. The mutex is never held while rings are stopped. An
unattached or non-shm reply stream stays fatal. The context's ID and debug
name are added to the "destroyed while ... uses it" lines.

Not reproduced deterministically: the interleaving needs a guest ring
thread; no host-only ring harness exists. reply-resource.py and
context-diagnostics.py pass with this patch.

Generated-by: LLM
